.env
node_modules/
dist/
*.db*
*.sqlite
.expo/

# Firebase. Neither of these belongs in a PUBLIC repository.
#
# The *-adminsdk-* key can send push as the whole project and lives only in
# Expo's credential store. google-services.json is not a credential -- a copy
# ships inside every APK -- but an `AIzaSy...` key visible in a public repo
# reads as a mistake whatever the restrictions say, so EAS holds it as the
# file secret GOOGLE_SERVICES_JSON and app.config.js reads the path from
# there. Keep a local copy beside app.json for local builds.
*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json
app/google-services.json
